    "description": "Run the spec critic for one round\n\n## Summary\n\nCrew's spec critic now reviews a spec once. Before, a blocking finding sent the spec back to a writer and to a second critic round, up to two rounds. Records of 81 reviewed specs show that the second round found a blocking problem in about 1 report of 7, and each one cost a writer, an Opus critic and about 5 more findings to sort. Now the project lead fixes every accepted finding in the spec itself, blocking ones included, logs the declined ones with reasons, and goes on.\n\n**Ticket:** [T88 — Run the spec critic for one round](https://github.com/jerridan/crew/blob/main/docs/tickets.md#t88--run-the-spec-critic-for-one-round)\n**Type:** Refactor\n\n---\n\n## Agent context\n\n### Authority\n\n- `docs/design.md` §15.148 (new): the decision, its figures, and the split critic open question. It replaces §15.118's two-round cap; the rest of §15.118 holds.\n- `skills/project-lead/SKILL.md`, \"Have the spec reviewed\": owns the one-round rule and the rule that a report counts and a reserved number does not.\n- `skills/project-lead/references/record-format.md` owns the `reviews/` names; `resume.md` owns the resume; `substitution.md` owns a replaced spec review.\n\n### What changed, by file\n\n- `skills/project-lead/SKILL.md`: \"Have the spec reviewed\" states one critic round. The project lead applies every accepted finding to `spec.md`, blocking ones included, logs the declined ones, and goes to the sweep with no writer round, no second critic round and no question. A critic that returned no report is dispatched again; a run adjudicates one report. The label table's `blocking` row names the project lead's own edit of `spec.md` for a spec critic finding.\n- `skills/project-lead/references/record-format.md`: `reviews/spec-critic-r<n>.md` is round 1 on a new run; a higher `<n>` comes only from a re-dispatch; `-r2` and `-r3` in older records stay valid history.\n- `skills/project-lead/references/resume.md`: a resume re-dispatches no spec critic that left a report, and adjudicates it if no adjudication is on record; a reservation file with no report means dispatch again.\n- `skills/project-lead/references/substitution.md`: names the verdict string `re-spec needed` in place of \"a re-spec\".\n- `agents/spec-critic.md`: says that no second round follows, and that the project lead fixes each accepted finding itself. Both verdict strings stay.\n- `skills/project-lead/scripts/crew-stats.py`: one comment; no code change.\n- `docs/design.md`: new §15.148; §15.118 points to it.\n- `docs/tickets.md`: new T88.\n- `CLAUDE.md`: Build state names T88's one-round rule.\n- `.claude-plugin/plugin.json`, `.claude-plugin/marketplace.json`: version 0.1.115.\n\n### Constraints that applied\n\n- Version rule: the change touches `skills/` and `agents/`, so both manifests go to 0.1.115, the same value.\n- One rule, one file: `SKILL.md` owns the round rule; `record-format.md`, `resume.md` and design §15.148 point at it.\n- The split critic is unchanged: `git diff origin/main -- agents/split-critic.md skills/project-lead/references/full-path.md` is empty.\n- The verdict strings stay, because `crew-stats.py` and old records read them.\n- `docs/implementation-plan.md` and `docs/stage-2-run/` are untouched.\n\n### How this was verified\n\n- `grep -rn -i -E 'two rounds is the cap|dispatch .spec-writer-r<n>. again|critic.s next round' skills agents` prints nothing.\n- `grep -rn -i -E 'two-round spec|spec critic .{0,40}two rounds|two rounds is the cap'` over the repo, less the frozen docs, `design.md` history and the new ticket, prints nothing.\n- `crew-stats.py` at `origin/main` and at this head, run on one frozen copy of the record root, print the same 244 lines except the USD figure of one live run, which `spend.py` prices from transcripts outside the copy. The script change is a comment.\n- `SKILL.md` is 490 lines, under its 500-line target.\n- A read of each changed file against the spec's eleven requirements and `writing-standard.md`'s \"Before you open the PR\".\n- The run that built this change used the rule on its own spec: the one critic report held 2 blocking and 8 other findings, and the project lead applied all 10 to the spec with no second round.\n\n### Known gaps\n\n- The split critic keeps its rounds. §15.148 records its figures as an open question: round 2 sends a split back in 3 of 16 reports, against 16 of 33 at round 1.\n- No other run has used the one-round rule yet.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01XrBTZgYWHHNhRSy3s6RFPj\n",
